WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.650
The kit's wave plan playbook
runs only on the control node.

2
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:05.013
You give it a wave number.

3
00:00:05.013 --> 00:00:09.924
It lists the wave's ready servers
and the ones the CMDB blocked,

4
00:00:09.924 --> 00:00:15.701
and writes a JSON and a CSV plan under
reports: host, configuration item,

5
00:00:15.701 --> 00:00:19.072
environment, resource
group, region, cloud,

6
00:00:19.072 --> 00:00:22.538
both owners, the exact
tag string and a state.

7
00:00:22.538 --> 00:00:26.247
It stops when no wave is given
or the wave has no ready server,

8
00:00:26.247 --> 00:00:30.032
when the cloud is wrong or a
region belongs to the other cloud,

9
00:00:30.032 --> 00:00:34.120
when a production server is planned
in wave zero or one, which this

10
00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:38.813
workbook's Arc track keeps for non-production,
and when a server has no owner.

11
00:00:38.813 --> 00:00:42.409
Both onboarding playbooks
import it as their first play,

12
00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:45.087
so if the plan stops,
no server is contacted.

13
00:00:45.087 --> 00:00:49.946
The playbook that uses Microsoft's role
runs in batches, one canary server,

14
00:00:49.946 --> 00:00:52.257
then five, then twenty-five percent,

15
00:00:52.257 --> 00:00:56.399
with the batch keywords the
Ansible documentation describes.

16
00:00:56.399 --> 00:00:59.625
It's in check mode unless you
set confirm change to true.

17
00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:03.400
Then the role isn't called, and each
server prints what it would get.

18
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.473
With the flag, the role runs
with the CMDB's values,

19
00:01:06.473 --> 00:01:09.290
authenticating with the managed identity.
